<h2 id=3D"ScrumTeamMPSYSSuite-WhatisMemberProfileSystem(MPSYS):"><strong>Wh=
at is Member Profile System (MPSYS): </strong></h2>
<p>The Member Profile System is the system of record for consumer and SMB i=
dentity management. MPSYS creates and stores user=E2=80=99s online identity=
, the user profile data such as the user ID, password, demographic informat=
ion, SLID linkage, and information on the products &amp; services the user =
currently is subscribed to. The Member Profile Data store is the authoritat=
ive namespace for allocation all new user identities. The Member Profile Sy=
stem provides APIs to support all AT&amp;T Internet Services, Uverse applic=
ations, DTV, Wireless and partners such as Yahoo and Motive to manage user =
Ids and user related information. This system also provides a transaction h=
ub (Resource Integration Layer) that houses all business rules and gates al=
l transactions to MPSYS, manages transaction distribution via a home-grown =
distribution bus (DBus) across various systems like Member Profile Store, N=
etwork engineering LDAP, MPS LDAP, HaloC, CustomerGraph, CCR, BBNMS, G2 and=
 third parties such as Yahoo, McAfee and Motive and keeps the member data i=
n sync across the disparate systems. MPSYS also handles account and identit=
y level fraud locking, manage OTP generation and validation for various onl=
ine and retail channels.</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>The Member Profile System supports the following products/services:</p>
<ul>
<li>AT&amp;T Internet Services such as DSL, Portal, Email</li>
<li>U-verse services such as HSIA, IPTV, VOIP</li>
<li>Mobility, Prepaid and Fixed Wireless Internet (WLL), Over the top Voice=
 (OTTV)</li>
<li>Bundled services for Uverse, DirecTV and Mobility</li>
<li>DTV Streaming, DTV satellite and other dynamic services</li>
<li>Wireline accounts</li>
<li>McAfee Internet Security Service (ISS)</li>
<li>Mobility Subscription (DMCTN) service</li>
<li>Association between accessId and INDIVIDUAL ID.</li>
</ul>
<p><br></p>
<p><strong>MPSYS-Subscription Services:</strong></p>
<p>Member Profile System Subscription Services is a sub application of Memb=
er Profile System. MPSYS Subscription Services manages Uverse Subscribers, =
Components, Users and the Associations between them. It manages Uverse comp=
onents that have been provisioned for a subscriber. Components include HSIA=
, VOIP and IPTV and also Mailbox, VoIPLine, VoIP Device, STB, Genre, WiFi, =
RG, WLL, DTV and Unified Mobility. It also manages settings established for=
 a user and components they control and the degree of control they the user=
 is given.</p>
<ul>
<li>Provisioning flow from LS-OMS (via BBNMS) initiates Access ID auto-regi=
stration and Uverse Member ID service provisioning flow</li>
<li>MPSYS-SS manages Uverse Subscribers, Components, Users and the Associat=
ions between them.</li>
<li>MPSYS-SS manages what Uverse components have been provisioned for a sub=
scriber. Components include HSIA, VOIP and IPTV and also Mailbox, VoIPLine,=
 VoIP Device, STB, Genre, WiFi and RG.</li>
<li>MPSYS-SS also manages settings that have been established for a user an=
d what components they control and the degree of control they have been giv=
en for MAILBOX and Address Book management.</li>
<li>MPSYS-SS manages basic information for unified mobility, Directv, Fixed=
 Wireless Internet (WLL).</li>
<li>MPSYS-SS manages AT&amp;T Phone Advanced (APA/OTTV) provisioning and au=
to-registration.</li>
</ul>
